      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolverton%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city was incorporated as a village on April 24, 1913, and separated from the township on March 10, 1936; the townsite in section 28 was platted in 1884.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://lakesnwoods.com/Wolverton.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The growth of the budding village was halted in 1889 when the railroad came through about one mile north on its way from Breckenridge to Moorehead.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.forgottenminnesota.com/2023/01/04/the-old-school-in-wolverton/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "When Miller’s Station was established in 1878, the small trading post town was a steamboat stop along the Red River with a post office, store, and elevator.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.forgottenminnesota.com/2023/01/04/the-old-school-in-wolverton/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The old Wolverton school originally had a central hall and a wing on the north side of the building with classrooms.",
